<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pyotr Rumyantsev</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Rumyantsev</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pyotr Rumyantsev was a Russian field marshal of the eighteenth century, one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catherine-the-great">Catherine the Great</a>'s leading commanders. He won major victories against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-turkish-war-1768-1774">Russo-Turkish War</a> of 1768–1774. His campaigns helped extend the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> towards the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pyotr-rumyantsev.jpg" alt="Pyotr Rumyantsev" width="320" height="385" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown artistUnknown artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%9F%D0%BE%D1%80%D1%82%D1%80%D0%B5%D1%82_%D0%B3%D0%B5%D0%BD.-%D1%84%D0%B5%D0%BB%D1%8C%D0%B4%D0%BC.%D0%B3%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%84%D0%B0_%D0%9F%D0%B5%D1%82%D1%80%D0%B0_%D0%90%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BA%D1%81%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%B4%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B8%D1%87_%D0%A0%D1%83%D0%BC%D1%8F%D0%BD%D1%86%D0%B5%D0%B2%D0%B0-%D0%97%D0%B0%D0%B4%D1%83%D0%BD%D0%B0%D0%B9%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%B3%D0%BE._%D0%93%D0%98%D0%9C_e1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
